# AudioWRT-owned packages that need OpenWrt development dependencies staged
# while compiling. This includes wrappers around upstream source and AudioWRT
# native C packages that include/link against OpenWrt feed libraries.
#
# Packages NOT listed here stay on the NO_DEPS=1 package boundary. Runtime-only
# OpenWrt dependencies must never turn into source-build roots.
#
# Wi-Fi ownership:
# - audiowrt-wpad compiles one multicall hostapd+wpa_supplicant binary from the
#   exact OpenWrt hostap source, but stays on the NO_DEPS=1 boundary.
#   scripts/build.sh stages only its required development interfaces from
#   exact-release sources/APKs so hostapd-common/ubus/ucode never become
#   recursive source-build roots.
#
# Bluetooth ownership:
# - audiowrt-bluez builds only the constrained bluetoothd daemon; runtime
#   libbluetooth comes from the official OpenWrt bluez-libs package.
# - audiowrt-btctl is AudioWRT-owned C code but needs glib2/GIO development
#   headers, so it uses the explicit development-dependency path.
# - bluez-alsa uses the official OpenWrt sbc and bluez-libs packages.

librespot
audiowrt-bluez
audiowrt-btctl
bluez-alsa
